    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This thesis examines the role of patent litigation in the generic drug approval process.\r\nGeneric drug companies wishing to enter a brand-name drug market early may challenge\r\na brand-name’s patents by filing for an Abbreviated New Drug Application (ANDA) with a\r\nparagraph IV certification. While anecdotal evidence on the characteristics of paragraph IV\r\nlawsuits abound, there has yet to be a comprehensive study on these unique cases. Leveraging\r\na new dataset of district court cases, this thesis presents an empirical investigation\r\ninto some of the current trends in generic drug litigation from January 1, 2006 to August 1,\r\n2011. Using several basic econometric specifications, I study the determinants of settlement\r\nand other outcomes in these cases, observing that factors such as declaratory judgment, the\r\nsize of a pioneer company, the level of patent protection, and remaining exclusivity may be\r\nsignificant factors.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Wang, X. (2022). Understanding Current Trends and Outcomes in Generic Drug Patent Litigation: An Empirical Investigation. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/cd855cc8889",
            "type": "preferred citation",
